
1. Clean build on the fixture lineage
  PASS  1.1 the eligible frame is the non-census v2 bridges minus the v1 sample minus the adjudicated pack
  PASS  1.2 the ranking is sha256(salt|url) ascending, ties by url (independent computation)
  PASS  1.3 the rows are the first n ranked persons with ordinals 1..n
  PASS  1.4 every selection_key equals export_person_bridge.salted_key (v1 formula parity)
  PASS  1.5 the v2 census is derived from Stage A and equals the v1 census
  PASS  1.6 the frame accounting is exact
  PASS  1.7 disjointness from the census, the v1 census, the v1 random stratum and the adjudicated pack is proven and recorded as zero overlaps
  PASS  1.8 generated_utc is frozen to the validated child's generated_utc and the child is hash-linked with its validation summary
  PASS  1.9 every row carries the parent identity and the child status, and no verdict field
  PASS  1.10 the zero-failure bound is 1 - 0.05^(1/n), recorded beside n
  PASS  1.11 rows_sha256 is the sha256 of the canonical rows
  PASS  1.12 the CSV is LF-only with the declared header and one line per row
  PASS  1.13 a second build reproduces both outputs byte-for-byte
  PASS  1.14 a different salt produces different selection keys for every frame person
  PASS  1.15 no absolute path, DSN or credential appears in the outputs (the fixture root is an absolute temp path and is absent)
  PASS  1.16 every input and tool hash is recorded repository-relative

2. Frame options and refusals
  PASS  2.1 --include-adjudicated returns the adjudicated bridged non-census person to the frame
  PASS  2.2 n larger than the eligible frame is refused
  PASS  2.3 reusing the prior sample's salt is refused
  PASS  2.4 a salt containing '|' or a non-positive n is refused
  PASS  2.5 a v2 census that differs from the v1 census is refused (operator matter)
  PASS  2.6 a child that fails validation refuses generation (the gate)
  PASS  2.7 a pinned-input hash mismatch is refused before anything is computed
  PASS  2.8 the tool exposes no overwrite flag

3. Output lifecycle (validate-only writes nothing; write never overwrites)
  PASS  3.1 validate-only exits 0 and writes nothing
  PASS  3.2 validate-only reports both outputs absent with their would-be hashes
  PASS  3.3 write exits 0 and creates both outputs with the computed bytes
  PASS  3.4 a second write exits 0 and reports both outputs identical
  PASS  3.5 validate-only after a write exits 0
  PASS  3.6 write refuses when an existing output differs and touches neither file
  PASS  3.7 validate-only exits 1 when an existing output differs
  PASS  3.8 a refusal inside run() is reported, not raised, with exit 1

4. No database / network / import code path
  PASS  4.1 the generator imports no database, network, subprocess, GUI, importer or exporter module
  PASS  4.2 the generator reads no environment variable
  PASS  4.3 every frozen tool source exists in the repository
  PASS  4.4 the top-10 census helper module imports no network or database module either

5. Pinned Phase F constants
  PASS  5.1 the default salt is AFLDB-ISSUE-222/v2 and the default n is 598
  PASS  5.2 the ordering formula is the v1 formula with the new salt
  PASS  5.3 the outputs are the v2 validation-sample JSON and CSV under docs/rebuild-manifests
  PASS  5.4 the pinned inputs include the validated v2 child, the v1 review sample and the Stage A rows with the recorded hashes
  PASS  5.5 no output path is a pinned input path (nothing pinned can be overwritten)
  PASS  5.6 the sample never carries a verdict field and declares itself unreviewed

All DraftGuru validation-sample checks hold.
